abstract: "Two preprints on the Rado numbers of a(x-y)=bz (three-colour lower bound for all a<b, R_3(a,a+1)=a^3+5a^2+8a for a>=7, recursive lower bounds for every number of colours, reduction of the three-colour upper bound to one conjecture; R_4(3(x-y)=4z)=461, R_4(5(x-y)=4z)=741, R_4(6(x-y)=5z)=1501) with all programs and recorded results. Proofs checked by lrat-check and cake_lpr. Not peer reviewed."
keywords:
  - Rado numbers
  - Ramsey theory on the integers
  - SAT solving
  - cube-and-conquer
  - LRAT proofs
